{"step_index":331,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T06:53:34Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-09-01T06:53:34Z sender=9bf18d5c-546d-4033-a57a-8af2aed9cf74 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=```python\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport cartopy.crs as ccrs\nimport cartopy.feature as cfeature\n\ndef render_frames(start_frame, end_frame, total_frames=360):\n    # Coordinates for Washington D.C.\n    dc_lon, dc_lat = -77.0369, 38.9072\n    # Coordinates for New Delhi\n    nd_lon, nd_lat = 77.2090, 28.6139\n\n    geodetic = ccrs.Geodetic()\n    \n    # Generate points along the great circle path\n    # npts returns points *between* the start and end, so we ask for total_frames - 2\n    path_points = geodetic.npts(dc_lon, dc_lat, nd_lon, nd_lat, total_frames - 2)\n    lons = [dc_lon] + [p[0] for p in path_points] + [nd_lon]\n    lats = [dc_lat] + [p[1] for p in path_points] + [nd_lat]\n\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n    \n    for frame in range(start_frame, end_frame + 1):\n        fig.clf()\n        ax = fig.add_subplot(1, 1, 1, projection=ccrs.Robinson())\n        ax.set_global()\n        \n        # Add map features\n        ax.coastlines(resolution='110m', color='black', linewidth=1)\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.BORDERS, linestyle=':', alpha=0.5)\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.LAND, facecolor='lightgray')\n        ax.add_feature(cfeature.OCEAN, facecolor='azure')\n\n        # Calculate current path length up to the current frame\n        current_idx = min(frame, len(lons) - 1)\n        \n        # Plot path\n        if current_idx > 0:\n            ax.plot(lons[:current_idx + 1], lats[:current_idx + 1], \n                    transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), color='red', linewidth=2)\n        \n        # Plot current airplane position\n        ax.plot(lons[current_idx], lats[current_idx], \n                transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), marker='o', color='darkred', markersize=6)\n\n        # Plot start and end points\n        ax.plot(dc_lon, dc_lat, transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), marker='*', color='blue', markersize=10, label='Washington D.C.')\n        ax.plot(nd_lon, nd_lat, transform=ccrs.Geodetic(), marker='*', color='green', markersize=10, label='New Delhi')\n\n        plt.title(f\"Flight: Washington D.C. to New Delhi - Frame {frame}\")\n        plt.legend(loc='lower left')\n        \n        # Save the frame\n        filename = f\"frame_{frame:04d}.png\"\n        plt.savefig(filename, dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n        print(f\"Rendered {filename}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Render the requested frames\n    render_frames(271, 360, total_frames=360)\n```\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
